{"code": "import math\n\ndef predict(probe):\n    # Model of the black box f(x).\n    #\n    # Main idea: f(x) = sign(x) * floor(|x|)   for |x| < 5, and 0 otherwise.\n    # But there is a \"different region\" near |x| in [4,5]: instead of floor,\n    # values in that band map to 4 (for 4 <= |x| < 4.35) or 5 (for 4.35 <= |x| < 5).\n    # Let's check the evidence carefully.\n    #\n    # Observations:\n    #  - For small |x| (< 4): f(x) = trunc toward zero (floor of |x| with sign).\n    #    E2: -3->-3, -2.5->-2, -2->-2, -1.8->-1, ..., -0.6->0, 0.5->1, 1->1, 2->2.\n    #    E4: 3->3, 4->4, 5->0, 6->0 ... and -4->-4, -5->-0, ...\n    #    E14: 3.01->4, 2.99->3, 0.01->1, -0.01->-0, 2.5->3, -2.5->-2, 3.5->4, -3.5->-3.\n    #    E16: 0.999->1, 1.001->2, -0.999->-0, -1.001->-1, 2.5->3, -2.5->-2, 3.5->4, -3.5->-3.\n    #    E11: 1.4->2, 2.2->3.\n    #    E15: 0.6->1.\n    #    So for |x| < 4: f(x) = sign(x) * ceil(|x|)  ... wait check 2.5->3 (ceil), 2.99->3 (ceil),\n    #    3.01->4 (ceil), 0.01->1 (ceil), 0.6->1 (ceil), 1.4->2 (ceil), 2.2->3 (ceil).\n    #    And -2.5->-2? ceil(2.5)=3, sign*3=-3, but observed -2. Hmm.\n    #    Let's recheck E14: -2.5 -> -2.0. And E16: -2.5 -> -2.0. So negative side is different?\n    #    -3.5 -> -3.0 (E14, E16). -2.5 -> -2.0. So negative side: f(x) = -floor(|x|)?\n    #    -2.5: floor(2.5)=2 -> -2. -3.5: floor(3.5)=3 -> -3. -1.001: floor=1 -> -1. -0.999: floor=0 -> -0.\n    #    -3.01: floor=3 -> -3. -0.01: floor=0 -> -0. Yes!\n    #    Positive side: 2.5->3, 3.5->4, 0.01->1, 0.999->1, 1.001->2, 2.99->3, 3.01->4, 1.4->2, 2.2->3, 0.6->1.\n    #    So positive: ceil(|x|). Negative: -floor(|x|).\n    #    Check E2: -3->-3 (floor 3), -2.5->-2 (floor 2), -2->-2, -1.8->-1 (floor 1), -1.6->-1, -1.4->-1, -1.2->-1, -1->-1,\n    #    -0.8->-0, -0.6->-0, -0.4->-0, -0.2->-0, 0->0, 0.5->1 (ceil), 1->1, 2->2. Yes!\n    #    E4: 3->3, 4->4, -4->-4, -5->-0. Hmm -5 -> -0. floor(5)=5 -> -5, but observed -0.\n    #    So at |x| >= 5, result is 0 (except maybe boundary). E4: 5->0, 6->0, ..., 12->0. -5->-0, -6->-0, ...\n    #    So for |x| >= 5: 0.\n    #\n    #  - But wait, the \"different region\" near 4-5:\n    #    E6: 4.1->5, 4.5->0, 4.9->0, 4.99->0, 5.0->0. -4.1->-4, -4.5->-0, ...\n    #    E8: 4.25->5, 4.4->0, 4.45->0, 4.49->0, 4.5->0, 4.51->0, ..., 4.75->0. -4.25->-4, -4.4->-0, ...\n    #    E10: 4.3->5, 4.35->5, 4.2->5, 4.15->5, 4.05->5, 3.5->4, 3.9->4, 5.5->0, 6.0->0, 6.5->0.\n    #         -4.3->-4, -4.35->-4, -4.2->-4, -4.15->-4, -4.05->-4, -3.5->-3, -3.9->-3, -5.5->-0, ...\n    #    E12: 4.31->5, 4.32->5, 4.33->5, 4.34->5, 4.36->0, 4.37->0, 4.38->0, 4.39->0, 4.41->0, 4.42->0.\n    #         -4.31->-4, -4.32->-4, -4.33->-4, -4.34->-4, -4.36->-0, ...\n    #    E14: 4.349->5, 4.351->0, -4.349->-4, -4.351->-0.\n    #    E16: 3.999->4, 4.001->5, 4.1->5, 4.2->5, 4.3->5, 4.34->5.\n    #         -3.999->-3, -4.001->-4, -4.1->-4, -4.2->-4, -4.3->-4, -4.34->-4.\n    #    E18: 4.345->5, 4.355->0, 4.36->0, 4.365->0, 4.37->0.\n    #         -4.345->-4, -4.355->-0, ...\n    #         4.34->5, 4.35->5, 4.351->0, 4.349->5.\n    #         -4.34->-4, -4.35->-4, -4.351->-0, -4.349->-4.\n    #         4.3->5, 4.4->0.\n    #\n    #    So positive side: for 4 <= x < 4.35: 5. For 4.35 <= x < 5: 0. For x >= 5: 0.\n    #    Negative side: for -4.35 < x <= -4: -4. For -5 < x <= -4.35: -0. For x <= -5: -0.\n    #    Wait check -4.35 exactly? E18: -4.35 -> -4. So -4.35 <= x <= -4 -> -4. Boundary at -4.35 inclusive on -4 side.\n    #    Positive: 4.35->5 (E10, E18), 4.351->0, 4.349->5. So 4.35 inclusive -> 5. Boundary at 4.35 inclusive on 5 side.\n    #    So positive: 4 <= x <= 4.35 -> 5; 4.35 < x < 5 -> 0.\n    #    Negative: -4.35 <= x <= -4 -> -4; -5 < x < -4.35 -> -0.\n    #\n    #    Hmm wait, but E10: 4.05->5, 4.15->5, 4.2->5, 4.3->5, 4.35->5. And 3.9->4, 3.5->4.\n    #    So for 3 < x < 4: ceil = 4. At x=4 exactly: E4 4->4, E16 3.999->4, 4.001->5.\n    #    So x=4 -> 4 (like ceil(4)=4). For 4 < x <= 4.35 -> 5.\n    #    For 4.35 < x < 5 -> 0.\n    #    For x >= 5 -> 0.\n    #\n    #    Negative: -4 exactly -> -4. -4.001 -> -4. -4.35 -> -4. -4.351 -> -0.\n    #    -3.999 -> -3 (floor 3 -> -3). -4 -> -4 (floor 4 -> -4).\n    #    So -4.35 <= x <= -4 -> -4. -5 < x < -4.35 -> -0. x <= -5 -> -0.\n    #\n    #  - Large |x|: 0 everywhere (E1, E3, E5, E7, E9, E13, E17).\n    #\n    #  - What about |x| between 4 and 5 on negative side: -4.05 -> -4 (E10). -4.1 -> -4 (E16). -4.2 -> -4.\n    #    -4.3 -> -4. -4.34 -> -4. -4.345 -> -4. -4.349 -> -4. -4.35 -> -4. -4.351 -> -0.\n    #    So -4.35 is the boundary.\n    #\n    #  - What about positive 4.35 exactly: E10 4.35->5, E18 4.35->5. So inclusive.\n    #\n    #  - What about 4.34 vs 4.35: E18 4.34->5, 4.35->5, 4.351->0. So boundary at 4.35.\n    #\n    #  - Also check E6: 4.1->5 (yes, 4<4.1<=4.35). 4.5->0 (yes, >4.35). -4.1->-4 (yes, -4.35<=-4.1<=-4).\n    #    -4.5->-0 (yes, -5<-4.5<-4.35).\n    #\n    #  - Check E8: 4.25->5 (yes). 4.4->0 (yes). -4.25->-4 (yes). -4.4->-0 (yes).\n    #\n    #  - Check E12: 4.31->5, 4.34->5, 4.36->0. Yes.\n    #\n    #  - Check E14: 4.349->5, 4.351->0. Yes. -4.349->-4, -4.351->-0. Yes.\n    #\n    #  - Check E16: 3.999->4 (ceil 4), 4.001->5 (in 4<x<=4.35). Yes.\n    #    -3.999->-3 (floor 3 -> -3), -4.001->-4 (in -4.35<=x<=-4). Yes.\n    #\n    #  - Check E18: 4.345->5, 4.355->0. Yes. -4.345->-4, -4.355->-0. Yes.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 0? E2 0->0. E14 0.01->1, -0.01->-0. So 0->0.\n    #\n    #  - What about x in (0,1)? ceil -> 1. E14 0.01->1, E15 0.6->1. Yes.\n    #    x in (-1,0)? -floor -> -0. E2 -0.8->-0. Yes.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 1? E2 1->1, E16 0.999->1, 1.001->2. So 1->1 (ceil(1)=1).\n    #    x exactly -1? E2 -1->-1, E16 -0.999->-0, -1.001->-1. So -1->-1 (floor(1)=1 -> -1).\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 3? E4 3->3 (ceil 3). -3->-3 (floor 3 -> -3).\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 4? E4 4->4 (ceil 4=4). -4->-4 (floor 4 -> -4).\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 5? E4 5->0, E6 5.0->0. -5->-0 (E4 -5->-0).\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly -5? E4 -5->-0.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 4.35? E10 4.35->5, E18 4.35->5. So 5.\n    #    x exactly -4.35? E18 -4.35->-4. So -4.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 4.5? E6 4.5->0, E8 4.5->0. So 0.\n    #    x exactly -4.5? E6 -4.5->-0, E8 -4.5->-0. So -0.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly 4.351? E14 4.351->0. So >4.35 -> 0.\n    #\n    #  - What about x exactly -4.351? E14 -4.351->-0. So < -4.35 -> -0.\n    #\n    #  - Now what about 4.35 < x < 5: 0. And x >= 5: 0. So effectively for x > 4.35: 0 (up to infinity).\n    #    But wait, what about x between 4.35 and 5? 0. x >= 5? 0. So for all x > 4.35: 0? Let's check E1: 88.9->0, 67.5->0. Yes.\n    #    But what about x = 4.36? E12 4.36->0. Yes.\n    #\n    #    Hmm, but is there any nonzero for x > 4.35? All evidence says 0.\n    #\n    #  - Negative: for x < -4.35: -0 (i.e., 0). For x <= -5: -0. So for all x < -4.35: 0.\n    #\n    #  - So the function:\n    #    if x > 4.35: 0\n    #    elif 4 < x <= 4.35: 5\n    #    elif 0 < x <= 4: ceil(x)  [but at x=4, ceil(4)=4, consistent]\n    #    elif x == 0: 0\n    #    elif -4 <= x < 0: -floor(|x|) = -floor(-x)... wait let's be careful.\n    #         For -4 <= x < 0: f(x) = -floor(|x|)? Check -0.5: floor(0.5)=0 -> -0. Yes. -1.5: floor(1.5)=1 -> -1. Yes.\n    #         But what about -4 <= x < -4.35? That's x < -4.35, already handled.\n    #         Actually -4.35 <= x <= -4: -4. So for -4.35 <= x < 0: -floor(|x|)? Check -4.1: floor(4.1)=4 -> -4. Yes.\n    #         -4.35: floor(4.35)=4 -> -4. Yes. -4.351: floor(4.351)=4 -> -4, but observed -0. So boundary.\n    #    elif -4.35 <= x < 0: -floor(|x|)  [but at x=-4, -floor(4)=-4, consistent]\n    #    elif x < -4.35: 0\n    #\n    #    Wait, but for -4.35 <= x < 0, -floor(|x|) gives:\n    #    -0.5 -> -0, -1.5 -> -1, -2.5 -> -2, -3.5 -> -3, -4 -> -4, -4.1 -> -4, -4.3 -> -4, -4.35 -> -4.\n    #    All consistent.\n    #\n    #    And for 0 < x <= 4: ceil(x) gives:\n    #    0.5->1, 1->1, 1.5->2, 2->2, 2.5->3, 3->3, 3.5->4, 4->4.\n    #    All consistent.\n    #\n    #    And 4 < x <= 4.35: 5.\n    #    And x > 4.35: 0.\n    #    And x < -4.35: 0.\n    #\n    #    But wait, what about x exactly 0? 0.\n    #\n    #    What about very small positive x like 0.001? ceil -> 1. E14 0.01->1. Yes.\n    #    What about very small negative x like -0.001? -floor(0.001) = -0 = 0. E14 -0.01->-0. Yes.\n    #\n    #    So the model is complete.\n    #\n    #    Let me double check E2: -3->-3 (floor 3 -> -3), -2.5->-2 (floor 2 -> -2), -2->-2, -1.8->-1, -1.6->-1, -1.4->-1,\n    #    -1.2->-1, -1->-1, -0.8->-0, -0.6->-0, -0.4->-0, -0.2->-0, 0->0, 0.5->1, 1->1, 2->2. All match.\n    #\n    #    E4: 3->3, 4->4, 5->0, 6->0, ..., 12->0. -4->-4, -5->-0, -6->-0, ..., -13->-0. All match.\n    #\n    #    E6: 4.1->5 (4<4.1<=4.35), 4.5->0 (>4.35), 4.9->0, 4.99->0, 5.0->0.\n    #    -4.1->-4 (-4.35<=-4.1<=-4), -4.5->-0 (<-4.35), -4.9->-0, -4.99->-0, -5.0->-0. All match.\n    #\n    #    E8: 4.25->5, 4.4->0, 4.45->0, ..., 4.75->0. -4.25->-4, -4.4->-0, ... All match.\n    #\n    #    E10: 4.3->5, 4.35->5, 4.2->5, 4.15->5, 4.05->5, 3.5->4, 3.9->4, 5.5->0, 6.0->0, 6.5->0.\n    #    -4.3->-4, -4.35->-4, -4.2->-4, -4.15->-4, -4.05->-4, -3.5->-3, -3.9->-3, -5.5->-0, -6.0->-0, -6.5->-0. All match.\n    #\n    #    E12: 4.31->5, ..., 4.34->5, 4.36->0, ... 4.42->0. -4.31->-4, ..., -4.34->-4, -4.36->-0, ... All match.\n    #\n    #    E14: 4.349->5, 4.351->0, -4.349->-4, -4.351->-0, 7.5->0, 8.5->0, -7.5->-0, -8.5->-0, 20.25->0, -20.25->-0,\n    #    50.5->0, -50.5->-0, 3.01->4, -3.01->-3, 2.99->3, -2.99->-2, 0.01->1, -0.01->-0, 100.1->0, -100.1->-0. All match.\n    #\n    #    E15: -2.6->-2 (floor 2 -> -2), -120.4->-0, -116.9->-0, 52.1->0, 123.7->0, 23.9->0, -27.2->-0, -84.4->-0,\n    #    0.6->1, 123.4->0. All match.\n    #\n    #    E16: 3.999->4, 4.001->5, 4.1->5, 4.2->5, 4.3->5, 4.34->5, -3.999->-3, -4.001->-4, -4.1->-4, -4.2->-4,\n    #    -4.3->-4, -4.34->-4, 0.999->1, 1.001->2, -0.999->-0, -1.001->-1, 2.5->3, -2.5->-2, 3.5->4, -3.5->-3. All match.\n    #\n    #    E18: 4.345->5, 4.355->0, 4.36->0, 4.365->0, 4.37->0, -4.345->-4, -4.355->-0, -4.36->-0, -4.365->-0, -4.37->-0,\n    #    4.34->5, 4.35->5, 4.351->0, 4.349->5, -4.34->-4, -4.35->-4, -4.351->-0, -4.349->-4, 4.3->5, 4.4->0. All match.\n    #\n    # Great, model is consistent with all evidence.\n\n    xs = probe.get(\"x\", [])\n    ys = []\n    for x in xs:\n        try:\n            x = float(x)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            ys.append(None)\n            continue\n        if math.isnan(x) or math.isinf(x):\n            ys.append(None)\n            continue\n        if x > 4.35:\n            ys.append(0.0)\n        elif x > 4.0:\n            ys.append(5.0)\n        elif x > 0.0:\n            ys.append(float(math.ceil(x)))\n        elif x == 0.0:\n            ys.append(0.0)\n        elif x >= -4.35:\n            # includes -4.35 <= x < 0\n            ys.append(-float(math.floor(-x)))\n        else:\n            ys.append(0.0)\n    return {\"y\": ys}\n", "notes": "", "since": 18, "theirs": [], "ours": [], "fit": 1.0, "size": 653}